Subject: iOS: GE Plus's converted arenas live in Caches, not Documents

gexPlusRomConvert() writes the GoldenEye conversion into the first writable
of $E/mods and $H/mods, which on iOS are both Documents (patch 0009). That is
20 MB the game made itself, regenerated from the player's ROM in under two
seconds, sitting in the Files-visible, backed-up folder as a "GoldenEye
Arenas" folder the player never put there - the same reason 0009 sends
cache/ to Caches.

So on iOS $C/mods (Caches/mods) is tried first, both by the converter and by
the mod list that mounts the result (modListRefresh). If the system purges
Caches, the next launch converts again from the ROM behind the same notice;
if the ROM is gone by then, GE Plus says it needs one, as upstream does. A
conversion an earlier build left in Documents/mods is still found and used
where it is - nothing is moved or deleted.

Every other platform is unchanged.

diff --git a/port/src/gexplusrom.c b/port/src/gexplusrom.c
index dc6763d2e..a922b5e29 100644
--- a/port/src/gexplusrom.c
+++ b/port/src/gexplusrom.c
@@ -505,7 +505,15 @@ static s32 gexPlusRomConvertInto(u8 *rom, u32 romlen, const char *dest, const ch
 
 static void gexPlusRomConvertGoldenEye(void)
 {
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+	// $C (Caches) first: the arenas are 20 MB the game made itself and can make
+	// again in two seconds from the ROM, so they belong with cache/ and not in
+	// the player's Files-visible, backed-up Documents. A copy an earlier build
+	// left in Documents/mods is still found and used where it is.
+	static const char *const containers[] = { "$C/mods", "$E/mods", "$H/mods" };
+#else
 	static const char *const containers[] = { "$E/mods", "$H/mods" };
+#endif
 	// data/ is where the ROM went before added-content/ existed
 	static const char *const romdirs[] = { FS_ADDED_CONTENT_SEARCH, "$B" };
 	struct romsearch search = { "" };
diff --git a/port/src/mod.c b/port/src/mod.c
index 81b614826..8f90f82d6 100644
--- a/port/src/mod.c
+++ b/port/src/mod.c
@@ -3482,7 +3482,12 @@ static bool modListRootIsRepeat(const char *const dirs[], s32 index)
 
 void modListRefresh(void)
 {
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+	// Caches/mods holds GE Plus's converted arenas on iOS (gexplusrom.c)
+	static const char *const containers[] = { "$C/" MOD_MODS_DIR, "$E/" MOD_MODS_DIR, "$H/" MOD_MODS_DIR, "./" MOD_MODS_DIR };
+#else
 	static const char *const containers[] = { "$E/" MOD_MODS_DIR, "$H/" MOD_MODS_DIR, "./" MOD_MODS_DIR };
+#endif
 	static const char *const loose[] = { "$E", "." };
 
 	numModsListed = 0;
